(103, 'policy_privacy_content', '<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>\r\n<p><strong>Academy of Commercial &amp; Supply Chain (ACS Academy)</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>Last Updated:</strong> 28 October 2026</p>\r\n<h2>1. Introduction</h2>\r\n<p>ACS|Academy of Commercial & Supply Chain (\"ACS|Academy of Commercial & Supply Chain.,\" \"we,\" \"our,\" or \"us\") is committed to protecting the privacy and personal information of our website visitors, learners, trainers, and other users. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, store, disclose, and protect personal information when you access our website, register for training, or interact with our services.</p>\r\n<h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>\r\n<p>Depending on how you use our services, we may collect your name, email address, phone number, professional background, organization, course registration details, payment confirmation or transaction references, feedback, and information you voluntarily submit. We may also collect basic technical information, such as browser type, device information, and website usage data, where applicable.</p>\r\n<h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>\r\n<p>We use information to manage course registrations, deliver training, communicate course schedules and updates, process or verify payments, issue certificates, respond to inquiries, improve our programs, maintain security, and meet applicable legal obligations.</p>\r\n<h2>4. Payments</h2>\r\n<p>Where course fees apply, payment information may be processed or verified through the payment methods or providers we use. We do not intend to collect or store payment card security codes or online banking passwords. Please use only our officially communicated payment channels.</p>\r\n<h2>5. Sharing of Information</h2>\r\n<p>We do not sell personal information. We may share relevant information with authorized trainers, service providers, payment providers, or technology platforms when necessary to deliver our services. We may also disclose information where required by law or necessary to protect our rights, users, or platform security.</p>\r\n<h2>6. Training Sessions and Certificates</h2>\r\n<p>Online training may use third-party meeting or learning platforms that have their own privacy policies. Sessions will be recorded only where applicable and subject to appropriate notice. Learner names, attendance, or certificate details will not intentionally be published publicly without an appropriate basis or permission, except where disclosure is required by law.</p>\r\n<h2>7. Cookies and Analytics</h2>\r\n<p>Our website may use cookies or similar technologies to support functionality, understand usage, and improve user experience. Where required, we will seek consent before using non-essential cookies. You can also manage cookies through your browser settings.</p>\r\n<h2>8. Data Security and Retention</h2>\r\n<p>We take reasonable administrative and technical measures to protect personal information against unauthorized access, loss, misuse, or disclosure. Information is retained only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes described in this policy, including training administration, recordkeeping, and legal obligations.</p>\r\n<h2>9. Your Privacy Choices</h2>\r\n<p>Subject to applicable law, you may request access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal information, or object to certain uses. Some records may need to be retained for legitimate administrative or legal reasons. You may also opt out of non-essential promotional communications.</p>\r\n<h2>10. Third-Party Services and Links</h2>\r\n<p>Our website or training activities may link to third-party services, including social media, video-conferencing, and payment platforms. We are not responsible for the privacy practices of those services. Please review their privacy policies separately.</p>\r\n<h2>11. Children\'s Privacy</h2>\r\n<p>Our services are intended primarily for students and adults pursuing professional development. If we become aware that personal information has been collected from a child in circumstances requiring parental consent, we will take appropriate steps in accordance with applicable law.</p>\r\n<h2>12. Changes to This Policy</h2>\r\n<p>We may update this Privacy Policy as our services or legal requirements change. The revised version will be published on this page with an updated revision date.</p>\r\n<h2>13. Contact Us</h2>\r\n<p>For privacy-related questions or requests, contact ACS Academy through the official contact details published on our website or official social media pages.</p>\r\n<p><em>This policy should be reviewed and adapted to reflect ACS Academy\'s actual practices and applicable laws before publication.</em></p>', 'text', 'frontend', '2026-10-25 01:49:28', '2026-11-06 13:40:49'),
(104, 'policy_terms_content', '# Terms of Service\r\n\r\n**Academy of Commercial & Supply Chain (ACS Academy)**  \r\n**Effective Date:** 28 October 2026\r\n\r\n### 1. Acceptance of Terms\r\nBy accessing our website, registering for a course, participating in training, or using ACS Academy\'s services, you agree to these Terms of Service. If you do not agree, please do not use our services.\r\n\r\n### 2. About ACS|Academy of Commercial & Supply Chain.\r\nACS Academy is a professional learning platform focused on Commercial Operations, International Trade, Import–Export, Trade Finance, Logistics, and Supply Chain Management. We offer educational programs, training sessions, workshops, and related learning opportunities.\r\n\r\n### 3. Registration and Participant Information\r\nParticipants must provide accurate and complete registration information. Registrations are subject to course availability, eligibility requirements, and confirmation. Participants are responsible for keeping their meeting links and account details secure.\r\n\r\n### 4. Course Fees and Payments\r\nCourse fees, payment methods, and deadlines will be communicated before registration is confirmed. Participants must follow the stated payment instructions. Registration may remain unconfirmed until payment is verified.\r\n\r\n### 5. Cancellation, Refunds, and Rescheduling\r\nCourse-specific cancellation, refund, transfer, and rescheduling conditions will be communicated before registration or payment. If ACS Academy cancels a paid course, we will communicate available refund or alternative arrangements. Refund requests will be assessed under the published course terms and applicable law.\r\n\r\n### 6. Training Delivery and Changes\r\nTraining may be delivered online, offline, or in a hybrid format. Schedules, trainers, content, and delivery methods may change when reasonably necessary. Material changes will be communicated to registered participants.\r\n\r\n### 7. Attendance and Certificates\r\nCertificates, where offered, are subject to the course\'s stated attendance, participation, assessment, and completion requirements. Registration or payment alone does not guarantee a certificate unless expressly stated.\r\n\r\n### 8. Intellectual Property\r\nCourse materials, presentations, recordings, logos, and other content are protected by applicable intellectual-property laws. Participants may not reproduce, sell, publish, redistribute, or commercially exploit these materials without written permission.\r\n\r\n### 9. Acceptable Conduct\r\nParticipants must behave respectfully, avoid harassment and disruption, and respect other learners\' privacy. ACS Academy may take proportionate action in response to misconduct that disrupts training or compromises safety.\r\n\r\n### 10. Privacy and Communications\r\nPersonal information will be handled in accordance with our Privacy Policy. Essential course-related communications may include registration confirmations, payment verification, schedules, changes, and certificates.\r\n\r\n### 11. Third-Party Platforms\r\nOur services may use third-party platforms for meetings, registration, communication, or payments. Their own terms and privacy policies may apply. ACS Academy cannot guarantee uninterrupted availability of third-party services.\r\n\r\n### 12. Disclaimers and Limitation of Liability\r\nOur courses provide educational and professional-development opportunities. We do not guarantee employment, promotion, business results, or specific career outcomes. Training materials do not replace independent legal, financial, tax, customs, or other professional advice. Any limitation of liability applies only to the extent permitted by applicable law.\r\n\r\n### 13. Governing Law, Updates, and Contact\r\nThese terms are intended to be governed by the applicable laws of Bangladesh, subject to mandatory legal requirements. We may update these terms and publish the revised version with an updated effective date.\r\n\r\nFor questions, contact ACS Academy through the official contact details published on our website or official social media pages.', 'text', 'frontend', '2026-10-25 01:49:28', '2026-11-06 13:40:49'),
(105, 'policy_refund_content', '# Refund & Cancellation Policy\r\n\r\n**Academy of Commercial & Supply Chain (ACS Academy)**  \r\n**Effective Date:** 28 October 2026\r\n\r\n### 1. General Policy\r\nACS Academy aims to ensure fair and transparent arrangements for course registrations, cancellations, rescheduling, and refunds. This policy applies to paid training programs, workshops, and other learning services, subject to any additional terms communicated for a specific course.\r\n\r\n### 2. Cancellation by Participants\r\nParticipants wishing to cancel a registration should contact ACS Academy through its official channels as early as possible. Refund eligibility depends on the applicable cancellation deadline and course-specific terms communicated before payment.\r\n\r\n### 3. Refund Requests\r\nRefund requests must include the participant\'s name, course name, payment date, and relevant transaction reference. Requests will be reviewed individually according to the published terms and applicable law.\r\n\r\n### 4. Cancellation by ACS|Academy of Commercial & Supply Chain.\r\nIf ACS|Academy of Commercial & Supply Chain cancels a paid course or workshop without offering a suitable alternative accepted by the participant, eligible participants will be offered a refund of the course fee paid or another appropriate remedy in accordance with applicable law.\r\n\r\n### 5. Rescheduling and Trainer Changes\r\nACS|Academy of Commercial & Supply Chain may reschedule sessions because of trainer availability, technical issues, operational requirements, or circumstances beyond its reasonable control. Material changes will be communicated to registered participants, together with available alternatives and applicable refund arrangements.\r\n\r\n### 6. Absence and Late Arrival\r\nParticipants are responsible for attending sessions on time and meeting the stated participation requirements. Absence or late arrival does not automatically qualify for a refund, subject to applicable law and any course-specific commitments.\r\n\r\n### 7. Duplicate or Incorrect Payments\r\nParticipants should report duplicate payments or incorrect amounts with the relevant transaction details. Confirmed excess payments will be refunded or otherwise resolved following verification.\r\n\r\n### 8. Refund Processing\r\nACS|Academy of Commercial & Supply Chain will communicate the expected processing arrangements after approving a refund. Processing times may depend on the payment provider or financial institution. Refunds will ordinarily use the original payment method where practicable.\r\n\r\n### 9. Legal Rights\r\nNothing in this policy limits legal rights that cannot lawfully be excluded or restricted. Course-specific terms will be communicated before payment.\r\n\r\n### 10. Contact Us\r\nFor refund or cancellation requests, contact ACS|Academy of Commercial & Supply Chain through the official contact details published on our website or official social media pages. Never share passwords, PINs, or full payment-card security details.', 'text', 'frontend', '2026-10-25 01:49:28', '2026-11-06 13:40:49'),
